{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/98440-how-do-bloodlines-work-in-blood-smoke","id":98440,"title":"How do Bloodlines work in Blood & Smoke?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-25T10:19:42-07:00","id":98440,"title":"How do Bloodlines work in Blood & Smoke?","content":"I've seen the two example Bloodlines out already, and I was wondering if anyone had any idea when we might see more info on how to convert Bloodlines/guidelines for their &quot;gifts&quot; (especially since it seems they both get a 4th Discipline <i>and </i>a gift?).<br /> <br /> Oh, and do they cost anything to join now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:44:12-07:00","id":98763,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines no longer cost a Willpower dot as they used to in Requiem. There is still a blood potency requirement depending on connection to one's Sire, Avus, Clan, or wanting to found a Bloodline on your own, and needing to take Vitae from the Avus if you're not the founder (with all that entails).<br /> <br /> That aside, so far there's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions\">a thread around here</a> that at least covers trying to convert old Bloodline disciplines. Beyond that, nothing solid yet, but perhaps we'll see more about Bloodlines in the near future. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In the meantime, of course, there's always opportunity for people to try coming up with Gifts (and possibly tweaking the weaknesses) to complement the old list of Bloodlines that are around from Requiem . . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 03-25-2014, 08:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T17:35:32-07:00","id":98817,"title":"","content":"From what we've seen, bloodlines always have a &quot;gift&quot; a &quot;free something&quot; and access to special things. I think that the Neglatu were more of an exception in that they don't have a new discipline or devotions. Most bloodlines will prolly have devotions, given that David said new disciplines are rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Historian ~ <b><a href=\"http://www.nwodbrasil.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">www.cronistasdastrevasbr.com</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>I currently ST a... </b>MtAW 2e campaign called &quot;Axis Mundi - Si Vis Pacem&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/250-yuukale","name":"Yuukale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T19:21:53-07:00","id":98869,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines are currently being experimented on by the developers. Bloodlines get a 4th in-clan discipline as standard fare since they first came out. The current shift seems to be to limit new disciplines unless they actually do something really different than the core. Devotions work just as well to describe more of the bloodline discipline powers previously written. The easiest way to convert old bloodline powers would be to try to recreate them as devotions. If you keep getting stuck then they might need to stay a discipline. That would be more difficult to advise on a conversion, if necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T19:43:00-07:00","id":98882,"title":"","content":"It seems the Bloodline Gifts can be just about anything. Unique Disciplines, exclusive Devotions, changes to the vampire template, pretty much what ever is needed to express what the Bloodline does. For example, the Macellareus could just be able to gain Vitae by eating flesh and gain additional benefits for doing so, as a part of their template, rather than forcing Gustus to fit within the constraints of Discipline design. They still get a 4th discipline according to B&amp;S (I think Neglatu are kind of a special case because they're a Revenant bloodline instead of a Kindred bloodline). But they have more flexibility in what they can be, instead of only an additional weakness and a 4th discipline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T20:39:08-07:00","id":98910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/98440-how-do-bloodlines-work-in-blood-smoke?p=98882#post98882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems the Bloodline Gifts can be just about anything. Unique Disciplines, exclusive Devotions, changes to the vampire template, pretty much what ever is needed to express what the Bloodline does. For example, the Macellareus could just be able to gain Vitae by eating flesh and gain additional benefits for doing so, as a part of their template, rather than forcing Gustus to fit within the constraints of Discipline design. They still get a 4th discipline according to B&amp;S (I think Neglatu are kind of a special case because they're a Revenant bloodline instead of a Kindred bloodline). But they have more flexibility in what they can be, instead of only an additional weakness and a 4th discipline.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was very much my intention. If I did the Macellarius, I'd add to their template through gifts, not through Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T22:23:04-07:00","id":98954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/98440-how-do-bloodlines-work-in-blood-smoke?p=98910#post98910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was very much my intention. If I did the Macellarius, I'd add to their template through gifts, not through Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, glad to hear I had the right idea. There was one thing I would love if you could clear up for me though. According to the section on Bloodlines in Blood &amp; Smoke, all bloodlines have 4 Disciplines (although they don't always have to line up with their parent Clan's Disciplines). But the first Bloodline we got to see broke this rule. Is it still safe to assume that the default will be for Bloodlines to have 4 Disciplines, and cases like the Neglatu will be a rare exception? or is it less that &quot;all Bloodlines have 4 Disciplines (except a few)&quot; so much as &quot;sometimes Bloodlines can have 4 Disciplines, but they don't always&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T23:06:49-07:00","id":98970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/98440-how-do-bloodlines-work-in-blood-smoke?p=98954#post98954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome, glad to hear I had the right idea. There was one thing I would love if you could clear up for me though. According to the section on Bloodlines in Blood &amp; Smoke, all bloodlines have 4 Disciplines (although they don't always have to line up with their parent Clan's Disciplines). But the first Bloodline we got to see broke this rule. Is it still safe to assume that the default will be for Bloodlines to have 4 Disciplines, and cases like the Neglatu will be a rare exception? or is it less that &quot;all Bloodlines have 4 Disciplines (except a few)&quot; so much as &quot;sometimes Bloodlines can have 4 Disciplines, but they don't always&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neglatu are a rare exception. This comes from the fact that they effectively come from clanless vampires. However, I'd say take their clan spread once uplifted, and add Resilience, Celerity, or Obfuscate as a fourth option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T00:54:17-07:00","id":99015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/98440-how-do-bloodlines-work-in-blood-smoke?p=98910#post98910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was very much my intention. If I did the Macellarius, I'd add to their template through gifts, not through Disciplines.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be a neat rewrite, especially since there's that aside about Gustus possibly being a lot of smoke and mirrors on their part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:21:16-07:00","id":100237,"title":"","content":"So, here's where I'm not completely sure on the rules...<br /> <br /> The Bloodline's Bane is in addition to the Clan Bane, correct? And it takes effect upon a Kindred's joining said Bloodline <i>OR</i> when the Clan Bane would do for a neonate Embraced directly into the Bloodline?<br /> <br /> ...The fact that the first 'proper' Bloodline you unveiled was a Mekhet line (and yeah, one of my favourites, for what it's worth!) with a 'roving' Bane, I just wanted to make sure that I'm reading rules right. The Mekhet Bane isn't a set thing like the Ventrue or Nosferatu, and the Khaibit draft/sketch/post does make mention of mortals Embraced directly into the ranks of the Asps. Well, perhaps I'm more making sure that I'm reading rules as right as they are currently written? No joke, it's really an exciting prospect!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T12:34:57-07:00","id":100250,"title":"","content":"I think (but don't hold me to it) Bloodline Banes kick in when you're inducted (probably because their penalties aren't tied directly to Humanity as the Clan Banes are). Rose or Dave or Dave said this at some point. I <i>think</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T19:12:44-07:00","id":492189,"title":"","content":"I'm sure I've read it somewhere but I can't find it now ... if a Bloodline member is willing to teach their devotion to a non-Bloodline member, can they? Or must you join the Bloodline first?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T20:09:03-07:00","id":492238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laraqua</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/98440-how-do-bloodlines-work-in-blood-smoke?p=492189#post492189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure I've read it somewhere but I can't find it now ... if a Bloodline member is willing to teach their devotion to a non-Bloodline member, can they? Or must you join the Bloodline first?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an ST call. For what it's worth, MachineIV has said he'd allow it in his games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T20:21:42-07:00","id":492243,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Thought I'd read about it somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T06:40:24-07:00","id":504105,"title":"","content":"Its only my opinion (thus open to conflict, and the designers will always get the final word) but in my opinion Bloodlines should come in three levels depending on what the 4th discipline gained is, since when it boils down to it you are gaining an extra Gift at the cost of gaining another Weakness. From that theme and culture should be built and expanded as this would do two things:<br /> 1) Create some degree of mechanical balance between all bloodlines (greater power comes with greater cost - making every bloodline worth considering)<br /> 2) Theme is present and reflective of the gifts, instead of theme being created a gift jammed in just for the sake of having it<br /> <br /> From there the three tiers should then be as follows:<br /> <br /> - Tier 1 gives one of the five common disciplines (Animalisim, Obfuscate, Vigor, Celerity, Resilience). Since any Kindred can learn these without a teacher, they are a minor boon at best but can encourage some unique devotions from the combinations. As such the weakness from these Tier's would be on the equivliant of a minor Bane - meaning having this Bloodline would result in the Kindred technically having a max of 4 Banes (3 as per normal max, plus the 4th from their Bloodline). Due to this design there will only be a total of 15 of these Bloodlines since each Clan already has x2 of these common disciplines.<br /> <br /> - Tier 2 gives one of the five clan disciplines (Auspex, Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare, Protean) - a discipline and Kindred can learn provided they drink the blood of that clan member and be taught how to use the skill (coming with the penalties that follow in doing so). Having this discipline means you can learn it without risk of vinaculum, leading to some very powerful devotions. As such, these Bloodlines should usually gain a weakness akin to almost a Clan weakness - indeed a simple version of creating these Bloodlines would be to have the Clan weakness associated with the 4th discipline (e.g.: a Bloodline with Auspex + Dominate would have the Clan Weakness's of a Ventrue and Mekhet)<br /> <br /> - Tier 3 offers a completely new and unique discipline - one that none outside the Bloodline can learn, and likely producing effects that rival the five clan disciplines (and sometimes even surpassing it). For this great power should come great cost - the weakness's of these Bloodlines should often be to a Clan weakness, what a Clan weakness is to a minor Bane. Such is the cost for power. Naturally this may discourage Kindred from using it, but then the temptation of power can be hard to resist.<br /> <br /> Thats just my take on it anyway. I'm sure I'm probably the minor in thinking this design is functional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T07:02:20-07:00","id":504110,"title":"","content":"Honestly can't say I dislike this idea. It sounds... tidy. But what about bloodlines that lose an affinity for <i>two</i> new ones? Those are/were a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T07:23:19-07:00","id":504117,"title":"","content":"True. I know they exist (though can't recall any right now damn it - mind blank <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) so they would be a case-by-case basis. If I had to throw an immediate thought/ response to it, I'd say base it on the disciplines in question. If they loose their Clan discipline to gain four non-clan disciplines, they'd probably have something even LESS of a Bane (such as 5-humanity for the penalty) as their new weakness since the Bloodline has actually LOST some power.<br /> <br /> On the cases where it simply swaps one common discipline for another, while gaining a second Clan disicpline (e.g.: a Daeva with Majesty, Dominate, Vigor, Obfuscate.... for whatever reason) would simply still get the Clan-Weakness level disadvantage as the power has shifted but not really be gained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:23:50-07:00","id":504428,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that bloodlines can also provide other boons than just the new Discipline. The bloodlines posted on the blog had everything from new Devotion, to new Merits or changes to parts of the Vampiric template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T12:58:44-07:00","id":504527,"title":"","content":"I dislike the idea greatly. It feels... limiting. It feels to insert rules and guidelines where there is none needed. And that's very apparent with tier 1 description, where it's even calculated the total number of bloodlines. What? You mean there can't be two separate bloodlines with the same discipline, but different backgrounds/bane/gift?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T13:35:02-07:00","id":504562,"title":"","content":"Well, just to make it fair, the number of possible tier 2 combos is 19. <br /> <br /> But yeah, the weirder stuff in 2e is going to diversify that pool nicely. I liked it just because it gave a framework to hang ideas off. No need to follow it religiously or anything. I like guidelines. If I could come up with this stuff on my own I wouldn't need to buy the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T13:48:10-07:00","id":504575,"title":"","content":"Griautis is correct - you can have two different Daeva bloodlines who pick up Dominate, for example. How they relate to that Discipline should be different in some fashion, presumably connected to their culture/background. <br /> <br /> I quibble with his '<i>guidelines where none are needed</i>' bit. While yes, the standard game for B&amp;S is supposed to be a small table of adult players who trust each other, that's not necessarily the reality for everyone. Putting aside dysfunctional tables, when you have larger scale convention, LARP or online games, some balancing mechanism is useful to encourage diversity. Drama aside, some bloodlines are objectively worse than other ones.<br /> <br /> I think as a substitute for &quot;<i>just work out balance / theme concerns with your table,</i>&quot; your idea has merit as a balancing system for new lines. Unfortunately, I think it would be a lot of work to try and go back and shoehorn older and the more recently blog'd bloodlines into that paradigm. Since Requiem is meant as a toolbox, we're getting cool and interesting tools that people are free to use or not, but some tools are going to be better than others in both a general way, and are going to be better in different styles of specific campaigns. <br /> <br /> I've seen more success in an overlay system of balancing Bloodlines. Where there is just a value judgment assigned by the Storyteller on each special snowflake item (Bloodlines, alternate Sorceries, Crazy Devotions, Hollow Mekhet, etc). And each player gets a limited number of those. Whether they come across as Merit Dots or Rarity Slots, you balance it with the overlay rather than trying to tune each thing individually. Ends up meaning if you want some crazy Bhumisparsa defense bonus that's going to be very powerful in your campaign, it will eat up most of your points. If you just want a Mekhet bloodline with Resilience In-Clan, that's a lot cheaper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T15:33:19-07:00","id":504681,"title":"","content":"Balance for the Storyteller system is better done through the gut and peer review than some formula, especially for a system that is meant to represent abnormalities.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I'm all for game balance (perhaps even too much so), but in my experience templateing the process in any way will close out good concepts without actually stopping all of the bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T19:21:17-07:00","id":504941,"title":"","content":"I probably should have pointed out this suggestion was indeed intended for balance in LARP groups predominantely where there are often too many numbers to monitor and the ST's need to be a bit more brutal in what they allow. Its also more of a quick band-aid response for now since there is a lack of many official Bloodlines for 2.0.<br /> <br /> I will probably follow this pattern as it makes it quite easy to produce bloodlines and record them on my Wikia. I knocked off two of them last night with little fuss actually on this basis - the Toreador and Bruja. At the least its clay on the wheel for me to mold later on and add details as the concept grows.<br /> <br /> I do agree that limitations can be unwanted, but that said even if this system propsed was incredibly rigid and restictive, it would still produce 34 bloodlines in total which is a decent opening selection - especially when this isn't even utilizing unique disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:15:06-07:00","id":551292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/98440-how-do-bloodlines-work-in-blood-smoke?p=504105#post504105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its only my opinion (thus open to conflict, and the designers will always get the final word) but in my opinion Bloodlines should come in three levels depending on what the 4th discipline gained is, since when it boils down to it you are gaining an extra Gift at the cost of gaining another Weakness. From that theme and culture should be built and expanded as this would do two things:<br /> 1) Create some degree of mechanical balance between all bloodlines (greater power comes with greater cost - making every bloodline worth considering)<br /> 2) Theme is present and reflective of the gifts, instead of theme being created a gift jammed in just for the sake of having it<br /> <br /> From there the three tiers should then be as follows:<br /> <br /> - Tier 1 gives one of the five common disciplines (Animalisim, Obfuscate, Vigor, Celerity, Resilience). Since any Kindred can learn these without a teacher, they are a minor boon at best but can encourage some unique devotions from the combinations. As such the weakness from these Tier's would be on the equivliant of a minor Bane - meaning having this Bloodline would result in the Kindred technically having a max of 4 Banes (3 as per normal max, plus the 4th from their Bloodline). Due to this design there will only be a total of 15 of these Bloodlines since each Clan already has x2 of these common disciplines.<br /> <br /> - Tier 2 gives one of the five clan disciplines (Auspex, Dominate, Majesty, Nightmare, Protean) - a discipline and Kindred can learn provided they drink the blood of that clan member and be taught how to use the skill (coming with the penalties that follow in doing so). Having this discipline means you can learn it without risk of vinaculum, leading to some very powerful devotions. As such, these Bloodlines should usually gain a weakness akin to almost a Clan weakness - indeed a simple version of creating these Bloodlines would be to have the Clan weakness associated with the 4th discipline (e.g.: a Bloodline with Auspex + Dominate would have the Clan Weakness's of a Ventrue and Mekhet)<br /> <br /> - Tier 3 offers a completely new and unique discipline - one that none outside the Bloodline can learn, and likely producing effects that rival the five clan disciplines (and sometimes even surpassing it). For this great power should come great cost - the weakness's of these Bloodlines should often be to a Clan weakness, what a Clan weakness is to a minor Bane. Such is the cost for power. Naturally this may discourage Kindred from using it, but then the temptation of power can be hard to resist.<br /> <br /> Thats just my take on it anyway. I'm sure I'm probably the minor in thinking this design is functional.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I love this as a design guide! <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T06:24:33-07:00","id":551301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/98440-how-do-bloodlines-work-in-blood-smoke?p=551292#post551292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I love this as a design guide!</div> </div> </div> </div>The next bloodline we release doesn't fit any of these moods, unfortunately. It's unlike any bloodline published before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T07:54:22-07:00","id":551474,"title":"","content":"Do we <i>need </i> a model? Seems to me that we have a general idea, but hard rules will just get in the way of fun ideas. If you're doing a custom bloodline, you'll have to check for broken mechanics either way, so I don't see how much it matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:57:40-07:00","id":557309,"title":"","content":"Are the cross clan bloodlines from 1st edition still a thing?<br /> Or is retconned away?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T14:08:03-07:00","id":557313,"title":"","content":"Considering the design philosophy of 2e, I highly doubt it's &quot;retconned away&quot; so much as it's not been necessarily done yet (The Neglatu <i>could </i>be an example.) Given how they have no desire to restrict the creative ways to design Bloodlines, I'd bet good money it's more of a case of not having done any 2e Bloodlines that use that mechanic yet (again, aside from the Neglatu.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T22:48:21-07:00","id":583210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/98440-how-do-bloodlines-work-in-blood-smoke?p=100250#post100250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think (but don't hold me to it) Bloodline Banes kick in when you're inducted (probably because their penalties aren't tied directly to Humanity as the Clan Banes are). Rose or Dave or Dave said this at some point. I <i>think</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been wondering about this lately myself but hadn't yet found an &quot;official&quot; answer. Does the bloodline curse kick in upon joining the bloodline or when you drop below Humanity 7 just as with the clan curse? (Especially seeing as how some bloodlines would double up on core clan banes, e.g. the Moroi with Gangrel and Nosferatu curses.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 07-08-2015, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T06:39:43-07:00","id":593741,"title":"","content":"Upon joining. The weakness is often directly tied to the benefits in 2e (actually it was often before too). For the Moroi, it is easy. After joining and as soon as Humanity is below 7, both clan curses take effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}